  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-02-07T23:05:30.726Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat Version: \n2021.4.2p2 Build 1160\nSDK Version:\n2021.11.24.16.19\nDescription of the bug:\nSynced object pickup delay is about 3x longer after ownership is transferred back to original owner.\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\nI am able to repoduce this every try with the following steps:\nI've included the amount of time it takes for the action to sync to other players in the world.\n- 2 players in the same world.\n- Player 1 picks up a synced object. (~1 sec)\n- Player 1 drops the object. (~1 sec)\n- Player 2 picks up the same object. (~1 sec)\n- Player 2 drops the object. (~1 sec)\n- Player 1 picks up the same object again, and now it takes about 3 seconds for this to update on player 2.\nNow every time this object is dropped and picked up, it takes about 3 seconds for the pickup to sync to other players, no matter who picks it up.\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots):\nI've attached a screenshot of the object I am using to test. It is just a cube with the \"VRC Object Sync\" script and the \"VRC Pickup\" script. There are no other UDON graphs on the object.\nVideo demo:\nhttps://streamable.com/p0v25h",
